  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feed The Future Orora Wihaze</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Rwanda):  ..The Feed the Future Orora Wihaze activity (Raise Animals for Self-Sufficiency) will sustainably increase the availability of, access to, and consumption of animal-source foods (ASF), including chickens, pigs, goats, and fish, through the development of a profitable ASF market. Orora Wihaze will train livestock producers, provide market linkages, strengthen value chain platforms, scale utilization of tested market solutions and co-invest with businesses to de-risk investments in ASF. Orora Wihaze will encourage ASF consumption through nutrition education. Orora Wihaze will support the Government of Rwanda (GOR) to develop policies that guide operations of businesses in the ASF sector. The activity will also develop private sector led models to facilitate access to ASF services. The development of a profitable ASF market will improve food security, economic opportunities, and improve dietary diversity, which is an important contributor to tackling malnutrition.   . .$1 million of activity funding contributes to meeting the required &quot;microenterprise&quot; earmark of $9.6 million. The activity is also allocating $200,000 to promote gender equality and women empowerment initiatives, through the Gender Equity and Equality Action (GEEA) Fund. Orora Wihaze&apos;s work is closely aligned to GEEA&apos;s Priority 4: Promote Entrepreneurship, and Financial and Digital Inclusion, including through Trade and Investment.. .Orora Wihaze contributes to USAID&apos;s Country Development Cooperation Strategy Objective 3, &quot;Increase Inclusive and Sustainable Private Sector Driven Growth&quot; and to USAID&apos;s Global Food Security Strategy......</narrative>
  </description>
